    "notes": "Served with the \"Edit-heavy coding-solo - DSpark k=14\" recipe from hiceron/spark-qwen38-27b (https://github.com/hiceron/spark-qwen38-27b, main d097a95), started with its own command GMU=0.85 K=14 ./scripts/boot-bakeer-dspark.sh and the script unmodified. The script defaults IMAGE to spark-vllm:qwen38, a local image the recipe describes as eugr/spark-vllm:latest of 2026-08-14 plus ffmpeg; that image is not published, so IMAGE was set to eugr/spark-vllm:nightly-20260814 (repo digest sha256:ab895847, image id a0cb301789ef, the same id the recipe run log records for eugr/spark-vllm:latest), which reports vLLM 0.27.2rc1.dev88+gaa3100357.d20260814, transformers 5.15.0, FlashInfer 0.6.18 and torch 2.13.0+cu130. ffmpeg is only needed for video and image input, and these rows send text. Target unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 with no revision pin, resolved to main f0b7c9e7; DSpark speculative decoding against Doopeworld/Qwen3.8-27B-DSpark-vLLM (5 layers, bf16, resolved to ebaa0919) with 14 speculative tokens and probabilistic draft sampling; gpu-memory-utilization 0.85, max-num-batched-tokens 16384, prefix caching on, the native 262144 window, reasoning parser qwen3, tool parser qwen3_xml with auto tool choice, 2 images and 0 videos per prompt, environment VLLM_MARLIN_USE_ATOMIC_ADD=1 and VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_FP4=0, host network, port 8888 (the script default). Attention backend, KV cache dtype and max-num-seqs are left to vLLM, which chose FlashInfer and an fp8_e4m3 KV cache from the checkpoint kv_cache_scheme. The chat template comes from the target repository, so the served default is thinking on: the speed rows force thinking off per request with chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false, the eval rows use that served default. The server runs without an API key; the harness attached over HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8888 and sent a bearer header the server ignores."
